{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Two hundred she-goats and twenty he-goats.</b> Two hundred she-goats need twenty he-goats, and so for all of them — the males according to the need of the females. And in Bereshit Rabbah it expounds from here the mating-frequency (עוֹנָה) spoken of in the Torah: travelers — every day; laborers — twice a week; donkey-drivers — once a week; camel-drivers — once in thirty days; sailors — once in six months. And I do not know how to align this midrash precisely, but it appears to me that from here we learn that the mating-frequency is not equal for every man but according to the exertion placed upon him — for we find here that he assigned to every he-goat ten she-goats, and likewise to every ram, because they are free from labor, their way is to mate frequently and to impregnate ten females; and a female, once she has conceived, does not receive a male. But bulls, which are engaged in labor — to a male he assigned only four females; and to the donkey, which travels a long journey, two females to a male; and to the camels, which travel an even longer journey, one female to a male."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:45.228272694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}